Subject: [PATCH] roamd: leave MLO networks alone

A multi-link network spans several radios and hostapd builds its RSN from
the MLO security setup (sae-compat with RSN overrides). With 802.11r/k/v
added on top, the QCN9274 firmware of the Xiaomi BE7000 crashed and the
router rebooted. Skip wifi-ifaces with mlo=1 when provisioning.
---
diff --git a/package/roamd/src/provision.c b/package/roamd/src/provision.c
index 4a39b40..3d6a5d8 100644
--- a/package/roamd/src/provision.c
+++ b/package/roamd/src/provision.c
@@ -120,6 +120,13 @@ static void iface_provision(struct uci_session *u, struct uci_section *s)
 	if (roam_uci_bool(disabled))
 		return;
 
+	/* A multi-link (MLO) network spans several radios. hostapd builds its
+	 * RSN from the MLO security setup (sae-compat with RSN overrides), and
+	 * 802.11r/k/v added on top of it made the QCN9274 firmware crash on
+	 * Xiaomi BE7000. Leave such networks as they are. */
+	if (roam_uci_bool(uci_lookup_option_string(u->ctx, s, "mlo")))
+		return;
+
 	net = mesh_network_by_ssid(ssid);
 	roaming = !net || net->roaming;
 
